    "extracted text": "The STW-zeotype germanosilicates were synthesized under hydrothermal conditions using N,N-diethyl ethylenediamine as an OSDA. In a typical synthesis, 3 mL (43.3 mmol) of N,N-diethyl ethylenediamine and 0.05 g (1 mmol) of GeO2 was added to 0.06 mL water. The mixture was stirred using a magnetic stirrer until the germanium oxide dissolved. After adding 0.8 mL of tetraethyl orthosilicate (TEOS), the mixture was stirred for another 2 h at room temperature to hydrolyze the TEOS, followed by the addition of 0.072 mL of an aqueous HF solution. The molar ratio of the batch compositions was (0.5–3)GeO2:(0.6–10)Si(OC2H5)4:(14.5–58)SDA:(6.9–120)H2O:(0.3)HF. The final mixture (pH=7–8) was sealed in a 25 mL Teflon-lined autoclave and heated to 170°C under autogenous pressure for 2 days. The solid product was recovered by filtration, washed with distilled water using ultrasonic cleaning, and dried at 333 K overnight. All the samples were synthesized at 170°C for 2 days, except for samples 1–3 which were crystallized for 31 days. Pure STW-type germanosilicate was obtained from a gel composition of 1.0 GeO2:0.8 SiO2:43.4 OSDA:3 HF:(6–24) H2O at 170°C for 2 days.",
    
